<!--
  Santali, Ol Chiki script (ISO 639 "sat").

  ═══ READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING ANY LINE IN THIS FILE ═══

  These translations are authored, NOT reviewed by a native Santali speaker with mine-site
  vocabulary. docs/REVAMP_PLAN.md section 11 states this as a known limitation and it is
  repeated here so nobody working in this file has to go and find it.

  Santali has roughly seven million speakers concentrated in exactly the districts this app
  targets, and no speech engine supports it. That is why voice input is a fixed 19-word
  vocabulary recorded per site rather than general recognition, and why no language model in
  this class is ever asked to generate Santali - none of them can write Ol Chiki. Everything
  a Santali speaker reads in this app is authored text or a pictogram.

  Rendering: Ol Chiki needs Noto Sans Ol Chiki, which ships in AOSP from Android 10. That is
  the reason minSdk is 29. Below it, every glyph here renders as an empty box.
-->
